    {
      "id": "claim_d6429ae2497648c4b639a606b444526d",
      "statement": "CLI-side payload type inference is an ordered heuristic (Google/Amazon/Azure payloads, kubernetes/serviceaccount issuer, then sha/sans claims as JWK, then classic claims as OIDC), so introducing a new token payload shape can change how existing tokens are classified and consequently how CSR SAN defaults are chosen.",
